HELP = {'Authorized endpoint': 'HTTPS base URL for a team-approved OpenAI-compatible chat API. Sent requests may include your question and explicitly selected derived records. Do not paste a public website URL or an unapproved endpoint; never expose proprietary seismic data without permission.', 'Model ID': 'Model identifier accepted by the authorised API endpoint (e.g. a model name from its documentation). This is not your ChatGPT subscription or ChatGPT website URL.', 'Session API key': 'Secret API token used only for the current running Streamlit session. Treat as a credential. Never paste it into code or share it with other users.', 'Authorize this endpoint to receive my question and selected derived records': 'Privacy gate. Enable ONLY when the endpoint is approved for the project data. The copilot may send the question and selected read-only evidence to the external server; raw SEG-Y files are not attached.', 'Read-only evidence': 'Choose the dashboard dataset summary the GeoCopilot can inspect: available wells, log statistics, seismic/horizon QC, 4D attributes, opportunity candidates, or uncertainty. The calculation must exist before it can be retrieved.', 'Statistics well': 'Select the well for numerical summary statistics of available log curves. Missing or non-finite values are omitted; these are descriptions, not petrophysical interpretations.', 'Candidate IDs': 'Select up to four calculated candidate polygons to send for AI comparison. Internal candidate IDs remain stable; display labels OPP-01 etc. can change when the ranking is recalculated.', 'Clear conversation': 'Delete the GeoCopilot messages from this app session. This does not revoke an external API request or remove external service logs.', 'Baseline / monitor palette': 'Select the seismic display colors for both 1995 and 2006 using a shared amplitude range. Changing the palette affects visualization only, not the seismic samples or QC scores.', '4D difference palette': 'Choose the red/blue or alternate palette for monitor-minus-baseline amplitude difference. Red/blue polarity depends on the displayed color scale; never read color alone as oil or water movement.', 'Focus well': 'Jump the seismic navigation to the nearest mapped IL/XL for the selected well. Manual preserves your own IL/XL selection. Distance to nearest trace does not prove a valid seismic well tie.', 'Inline': '3D seismic inline number. Moving this slider selects a different inline section and updates its survey-map position. This is a survey grid index, not an Easting in metres.', 'Crossline': '3D seismic crossline number. Moving this slider selects a different crossline section and updates the survey-map position. This is a survey grid index, not a Northing in metres.', 'Vertical axis': 'Choose Two-Way Travel Time (TWT, milliseconds) or approximate True Vertical Depth Subsea (TVDSS, metres). Depth mode interpolates through a selected/borrowed checkshot and is NOT seismic depth migration.', 'Overlay all intersecting well positions on seismic': 'Show well positions that intersect or are projected close to the displayed seismic section. Projected positions need not coincide with a real seismic tie.', 'Seismic orientation': 'Inline = constant IL, crosslines along X; Crossline = constant XL, inlines along X; East–West fence = ordered well-oriented arbitrary line with full-width stacked baseline/monitor/difference panels.', 'Horizon preview overlay': 'Display one existing well-guided reflector preview on the seismic section. Picks follow local reflectors only approximately and need fault, phase and well-tie review.', 'Well log preview': 'Choose exactly one well for the mini log section. The display uses available LAS log values and a stated depth assumption.', 'Section': 'Select inline, crossline or East–West fence geometry for the geological QC section. Survey axis and well projections differ between the three options.', 'Show interpreted geological horizons': 'Select several named well-marker-guided reflector previews to overlay. Each pick is preliminary; available top/base markers come from files, never invented.', 'Show well-top labels': 'Show named measured marker tops at their time or depth position. If a checkshot is borrowed or no matching seismic trace exists, the marker has uncertainty.', 'Horizon search window (±ms)': 'Maximum TWT distance either side of the well-guided predicted reflector where the automatic picker may choose an event. Smaller values enforce a tighter well tie; larger values increase event-mistie risk.', 'Show trace cursor on map': 'Display the currently selected seismic trace location on the survey map. Cross-navigation is click/slider driven, not continuous mouse hover.', 'Trace cursor · moves selected location on map': 'Select a trace along the displayed seismic section; the matching IL/XL and mapped XY point are highlighted in the 2D context map.', 'View seismic line': 'Switch the visible seismic extraction section. Choose the appropriate geometry before interpreting well/top overlays and seismic polarity.', 'Wells to display (east–west order)': 'Pick wells for the E→W correlation. Positions are arranged by projected Easting, not well number, and the well-track X locations are fixed.', 'Section top (m TVDSS)': 'Upper visible depth limit in metres TVDSS. Smaller numerical depths display shallower geology. This is a viewer range, not a geological reservoir top.', 'Section base (m TVDSS)': 'Lower visible depth limit in metres TVDSS. Must be deeper than section top; this changes viewing bounds only.', 'Vertical expansion': 'Stretches the well-log visualization vertically for easier correlation. Does NOT alter LAS values, depths or horizon picks.', 'Track width expansion': 'Controls the apparent width of plotted well-log tracks relative to the section. This is display-only; wider tracks can reduce lateral white space.', 'Correlate tops': 'Select actual marker names to connect across wells in the section. Unmeasured correlations are assumptions and must be reviewed.', 'Flatten to marker': 'Subtract each well’s selected measured marker depth from its log display to align that marker horizontally. Relative flattening is a visualization, not restoration of paleo-structure.', 'Geological top': 'Existing geological marker to seed the baseline reflector tracker. Only existing measured marker names are listed.', 'Map detail (IL/XL)': 'Subsampling step in inline/crossline grid cells. Lower numbers produce finer maps but read more traces and cost more CPU/time; smaller spacing does not create new seismic resolution.', 'Reflector search window ±ms': 'Time half-window around predicted horizon where event tracking is allowed. Wide windows increase the risk of jumping from one reflector to another.', 'Display estimated depth (single reference checkshot)': 'Convert displayed TWT to approximate TVDSS using one checkshot. There is no lateral velocity model; avoid treating as validated depth structure.', 'Build baseline + monitor horizon previews': 'Run the automatic reflector picking for the selected marker and show both seismic vintages with sensitivity/QC. Previews are not final interpretation.', 'Seismic trace → map cross-navigation': 'Choose a trace and highlight its IL/XL and mapped XY location on the square survey position map.', 'Top TWT (ms)': 'Start of the analysis interval in seismic Two-Way Travel Time milliseconds. Must be shallower/earlier than base; defines which samples contribute to 4D attributes.', 'Base TWT (ms)': 'End of the analysis interval in TWT ms. Must be later than top. Expanding the window averages over more seismic events and may dilute reservoir response.', 'Reference top (ms)': 'Start of the non-reservoir QC window used to estimate seismic background repeatability. Verify stratigraphically; it is NOT automatically known to be overburden.', 'Reference base (ms)': 'End of the reference QC window. Needs valid live samples and separation from target interval for defensible cross-equalization.', 'Map attribute': 'Select the calculated 4D seismic quantity to display: signed amplitude difference, RMS difference, NRMS, repeatability, or other available attribute. Units and interpretation differ by attribute.', 'Map grid spacing (IL/XL)': 'Sample an inline/crossline grid at this step. A smaller step reads more data and may improve contour detail, but cannot increase true seismic resolution.', 'Calculate / refresh window map': 'Compute 4D attributes for the chosen TWT interval and sampling settings. Validate baseline/monitor common coverage and reference QC before interpretation.', 'Export map CSV': 'Export actual calculated attribute map as CSV with relevant axes. Not a replacement for QA/QC-accepted seismic interpretation.', 'Calculate / refresh 4D map': 'Recalculate selected baseline-minus-monitor attribute window and update 2D map. The result is a seismic comparison, not proven fluid movement.', 'Calculate candidate screening polygons': 'Group neighboring qualifying 4D map cells into screening candidate polygons. Low change does not establish untapped oil; review geology and repeatability.', 'Export candidate envelopes CSV': 'Save candidate extents and characteristics for audit. This is not a drilling target shapefile without validated CRS/geometry.', 'Top / base markers to visualize': 'Select any number of available geological marker surfaces and compare their time or depth structure in 2D/3D.', 'Vertical domain': 'TWT (ms) follows seismic recording time; TVDSS (m) is checkshot-derived approximate depth. Depth conversion uncertainty increases away from control wells.', 'Grid sampling (IL/XL)': 'Controls sampling density of the surface preview. 5 = many traces, slower; larger values = faster, coarser maps. It is not seismic bin size or interpreted resolution.', 'Pick search ±ms': 'Maximum time search around the predicted reflector for horizon tracking. Wider allows more relief but increases false-event picks.', 'Surface reflector polarity': 'Select positive peak, negative trough, or either. The correct event requires synthetic-seismic well-tie phase and polarity verification.', 'Show well trajectories / vertical assumptions': 'Display boreholes on the 3D horizon plot. Vertical assumption paths are NOT actual deviation surveys until inclination/azimuth, XY and depth datum are validated.', 'Show geological marker tops': 'Overlay measured well tops and labels in the 3D viewer. They are well constraints, not surface-wide confirmed picks.', 'Build / refresh horizon previews': 'Run and cache multi-horizon baseline/monitor preview picks under the current search, sampling, polarity and depth settings.', 'Top TVDSS (m)': 'Shallow displayed depth boundary for the well correlation, in metres below mean sea level (positive down). A viewing parameter only.', 'Base TVDSS (m)': 'Deep displayed depth boundary for the correlation; must exceed top. Does not modify well logs or interpreted tops.', 'Vertical exaggeration': 'Stretch the Z axis for readability while all well-track X positions remain fixed. Z exaggeration changes appearance, not actual thickness.', 'E → W wells': 'Which well-log columns appear, ordered geographically East to West. X spacing remains locked for vertical zoom and pan.', 'Highlight geological tops': 'Show and correlate selected measured geological markers across the well section. These lines are preliminary correlation interpretations.', 'Flatten marker': 'Align one chosen measured top across the multiwell section by applying per-well display shifts. Missing top = do not force a tie.', 'Show East–West seismic fence': 'Open seismic fence following the well-control path, stacked Baseline / Monitor / Difference vertically.', 'Fence vertical axis': 'Show East–West fence in TWT or approximate TVDSS; checkshot controls the latter. Note it is a display conversion, not full 3D migration.', 'Overlay wells': 'Select wells to annotate on seismic and location map. Outside-footprint wells remain located but are not treated as seismic matched.', 'Overlay GR': 'Show Gamma Ray log thumbnails near projected well traces. GR is not a fluid indicator; lithological fill is a screening convention.', 'Overlay well tops': 'Draw available measured geological tops near the corresponding wells on seismic panels.', 'Show all well positions': 'Display all 8 wells, including wells with uncertain or missing seismic coverage, using a coverage caveat rather than invented seismic.', 'Visible interpreted horizons (multi-toggle)': 'Select multiple seeded horizon overlays on the selected seismic section. The event tracking is preliminary and reviewed separately.', 'Preview well': 'Choose the well whose log panel is shown in Overview. Other wells remain available for location map and correlation.', 'Preview log': 'Select GR, resistivity, density, neutron, PHIE or saturation where available. Each curve has its own units and scale; use them for screening only.', 'View': 'Select the seismic viewer geometry on Seismic QC. East–West arbitrary fence spans the well line and uses stacked panels to avoid compression.', 'Visible top/base markers': 'Show several marker-based reflector interpretations on seismic QC. A base marker is only present if supplied independently in the well-top file.', 'Show GR overlays': 'Overlay gamma-ray data near wells in the seismic section; lithology screen, not a seismic inversion.', 'Show measured well tops': 'Overlay available well markers, preserving their source datum and any checkshot/trajectory uncertainty.', 'Review well': 'Select one well for checkshot consistency, marker QC and optional synthetic seismogram validation. Best ties use the well’s own checkshot.', 'Validated sonic curve mnemonic': 'Exact LAS mnemonic for compressional sonic slowness (e.g. DT). Check unit (typically µs/ft or µs/m) and sonic quality before using it to build a synthetic; a wrong unit invalidates the tie.', 'Ricker peak frequency (Hz)': 'Dominant frequency of the trial zero-phase Ricker wavelet for synthetic seismic generation. Compare multiple plausible frequencies and validate seismic bandwidth and polarity.', 'Calculate synthetic tie': 'Construct a synthetic from sonic and density plus checkshot and compare with baseline trace. Output is experimental until wavelet, log units, well position and datum are validated.', 'Validation marker': 'Choose a measured geological top for leave-one-well-out horizon validation. At least three independent reliable checkshot-controlled wells are required.', 'Reflector search radius (ms)': 'Maximum TWT half-window around a held-out marker prediction used for reflector picking; controls the picking-versus-mistie tradeoff.', 'Expected reflector polarity': 'Select peak, trough, or unconstrained event. Requires validated synthetic-to-seismic polarity; incorrect assumption can tie the wrong event.', 'Validate marker': 'Leave one well out of the structural trend and compare its predicted reflector against its real measured marker. Reports residuals and QC flags; not automatic geological proof.', 'Export processing parameters': 'Download the reproducibility manifest containing input stamps, chosen processing thresholds, windows and selected parameters for QC audit.', 'Reference start (ms)': 'First time sample of the supposedly non-reservoir repeatability window. Check whether this TWT range is actually outside any dynamic reservoir interval.', 'Reference end (ms)': 'Last time sample of non-reservoir repeatability window. Reference must have sufficient live common samples and be distinct from reservoir target.', 'Target top (ms)': 'Beginning of the reservoir/target TWT interval used to evaluate 4D changes. Must come before target base.', 'Target base (ms)': 'End of reservoir/target TWT interval for 4D analysis. Together with top controls which traces/samples are analyzed.', 'Maximum lag (samples)': 'Largest integer time-shift searched when aligning repeated seismic in the non-reservoir reference. More samples permit larger corrections but risk suppressing genuine effects; convert to ms using seismic sample interval.', 'Suspected padding run (0 disables)': 'Consecutive zero-sample threshold used to flag suspected SEG-Y trace padding or mute. 0 disables rule; real zero amplitudes must not automatically be excluded.', 'Reference NRMS limit (%)': 'Maximum allowed reference NRMS for local repeatability screening. Lower gate is more selective, may exclude valid cells; higher gate admits noisier data. This is a screening threshold, not probability.', 'Try bounded spectral matching': 'Estimate a constrained spectral/amplitude filter from non-reservoir reference, then compare held-out QC. Does not guarantee true survey wavelet equivalence.', 'Apply documented early-time mute': 'If survey acquisition/processing mute timing has been verified, exclude earlier samples rather than interpreting them as 4D change. Leave off if unverified.', 'Mask samples earlier than (ms)': 'Time cutoff (TWT ms) for known muted samples. Requires documentation of mute; otherwise it can remove live signal and bias QC.', 'QC module': 'Advanced QC modules: 4.1 footprint, 4.2 registration, 4.3 amplitudes/phase, 4.4 NRMS/predictability, 4.5 non-reservoir reference, 4.6 shifts, 4.7 cross-equalization, 4.8 mutes, 4.9 before/after, 4.10 confidence. Interpret acceptance flags as review heuristics.', 'Diagnostic trace': 'Choose one actual paired inline/crossline trace to inspect raw and corrected amplitude/phase time series. This does not change survey-wide metrics.', 'Extraction mode': 'Time window: TWT interval for both surveys. Depth window: convert selected TVDSS via own checkshot. Horizon-bounded: picks between two separately controlled markers. Affects target samples used to derive 4D attributes.', 'Extraction top TWT (ms)': 'Upper/start TWT bound for 4D seismic analysis in milliseconds. Smaller time = shallower; ensure it is within live survey samples.', 'Extraction base TWT (ms)': 'Lower/end TWT bound for 4D analysis. Must exceed top. Larger intervals may mix reservoir with non-reservoir reflectors.', 'Checkshot for depth-to-time conversion': 'Choose the well’s own checkshot to convert a requested TVDSS target interval to TWT. The same resulting time window is applied to both vintages; not a lateral velocity model.', 'Extraction top TVDSS (m)': 'Shallow bound of the depth-window extraction in TVDSS metres. Converted to TWT by selected checkshot without extrapolation.', 'Extraction base TVDSS (m)': 'Deep bound of depth-window extraction in TVDSS metres. Must be deeper than top and within the selected checkshot coverage.', 'Sample spacing in IL/XL': 'Sampling stride of survey bins in inline/crossline index units: 5 (higher detail/heavier), 10 (balanced), 15 (coarser/faster). This is not physical bin size.', 'Top interpreted horizon': 'Choose an existing marker-guided upper reflector surface to constrain a conformable reservoir extraction window. Requires minimum independent well control.', 'Base interpreted horizon': 'Choose an independently supplied and tracked lower reflector. Must be different from top and below it; nonexistent bases are never inferred from naming.', 'Mask early-time samples using verified mute': 'Enable only if mute/cut timing has been independently confirmed. Excluded early-time samples are removed from QC and attributes.', 'Mute before TWT (ms)': 'Cutoff TWT before which verified early mute is excluded. Setting too high can remove real shallower reservoir signal.', 'Calculate survey diagnostics': 'Run shared-vintage grid pairing, masking, repeatability and extraction QC. Review coverage table even if no cells pass QC; heavy calculation can take time at stride 5.', 'Attribute map': 'Choose the 4D attribute displayed over the survey grid (e.g. NRMS, RMS, amplitude delta, time shift, repeatability). Attribute sign, units and reliability must be interpreted separately.', 'Export attribute figure (HTML)': 'Download the interactive Plotly map HTML for external review. Check its data provenance before publishing.', 'Map inline': 'Map cursor inline grid index; together with crossline it identifies the selected seismic cell and drives cross-navigation.', 'Map crossline': 'Map cursor crossline grid index; paired with inline locates the diagnostic position on 2D map.', 'Use this trace in Overview and Seismic QC': 'Transfer selected map IL/XL into Overview and Seismic QC section navigation to examine the same area.', 'Low contrast cutoff': 'Threshold below which reservoir-to-reference 4D contrast is classified as low-change for screening. Smaller means stricter low-change candidates. Low change is not proof of unswept oil.', 'High contrast cutoff': 'Threshold above which a local 4D contrast is classified high-response. Higher threshold selects only strongest contrasts; these may still be acquisition noise.', 'Minimum cells': 'Minimum number of connected sampled IL/XL cells to make one opportunity polygon. Larger values remove small noise blobs but can miss small true targets.', 'Minimum PHIE (fraction)': 'Minimum effective porosity cutoff for interval reservoir screening. E.g. 0.10 = 10% pore volume; calibrate to reservoir and log quality.', 'Maximum VSHALE (fraction)': 'Maximum shale fraction cutoff for reservoir screening. E.g. 0.40 means at most 40% shale. Generic assumptions need local petrophysical calibration.', 'Verified projected EPSG code (optional)': 'EPSG ID of independently verified projected XY coordinate reference system in metres. Required for defensible polygon area (km²) and GeoJSON; wrong CRS gives false area/volume. Do not guess.', 'Use verified well proximity as a coverage score': 'Adds a proximity-to-well-control evidence component AFTER CRS/geometry validation. Near a well does not prove depletion or connectivity.', 'Proximity decay distance (m)': 'Distance scale in metres over which proximity-to-well-control score decays (approximately exponential). This is not reservoir drainage radius and cannot quantify sweep.', 'Export WGS84 candidate GeoJSON with OPP names': 'Export candidate boundary polygons transformed from a verified projected CRS to longitude/latitude WGS84. Output also has OPP display labels and provenance.', 'Enable user-defined hydrocarbon pore-volume what-if analysis': 'Enable non-validated scenario calculation HCPV = area × net pay × effective porosity × (1−Sw). Not oil in place, reserves or remaining recoverable oil.', 'Populate clearly HYPOTHETICAL example inputs for testing (not Angsi measurements)': 'Fill volume assumption editor with explicit synthetic training values. NEVER describe these as Angsi measurements or use as actual remaining oil evidence.', 'What-if simulations per candidate': 'How many bounded triangular Monte Carlo samples to draw per candidate (500/1000/2000/5000). More samples give smoother scenario percentiles but take more time; they do not create field certainty.', 'Scenario reproducibility seed': 'Fixed random-number-generator seed. Reusing same seed and parameters reproduces the same Monte Carlo scenario draws; it does not change geological uncertainty.', 'Candidate evidence card': 'Choose a candidate polygon to inspect every evidence component, missing data, ranking inputs and uncertainty. OPP labels can reorder after a new run; use internal ID for audit.'}
